  "interpretation": [
    "The 16-replay/10-million-cycle recipe reports about 1.30% to 1.51% higher GPU-event time than the 5120-replay/no-delay recipe on the same graphs. Batch length and delay change together; this is not a pure host-cost estimate.",
    "At fixed 16 replays, increasing delay from 10 to 40 million cycles changes median event ratios by about -0.112% and -0.035% for the two graphs. No equivalence claim follows.",
    "All 576 queued samples had pending start events after enqueue. All 288 plain samples had completed starts, which is inconclusive. No sample was excluded by query outcome.",
    "First/second-capture exploratory interval widths are about 0.73% to 1.18%. The contextual 0.65% scale remains unresolved rather than an acceptance threshold.",
    "This calibration does not negate the much larger 18.9% to 22.0% explicit-winner regressions with different BMM kernels in the prior fixed study."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Six fresh processes are inferential units, not24rounds or144dependent batches.",
    "Queued wall spans include deliberate delay and are diagnostic, not serving latency.",
    "5120/noqueue versus16/queued compares complete recipes, not pure host submission cost.",
    "Prequeue delay can change device state;10m/40m sensitivity is not an isolated causal mechanism.",
    "Start.query True is inconclusive and retained; no outcome-based filtering/retries.",
    "Bootstrap intervals are exploratory/unadjusted and crossing1 does not establish equivalence.",
    "A single static-calibrated FP8 fixture/H100 does not establish fullmodel or universal ranking behavior."
